# Copy this file to .env and set the path for your machine.
#
# NEMO_EXP_DIR is where the training stack writes experiment output:
# checkpoints, .nemo exports and tensorboard events, under
# $NEMO_EXP_DIR/<exp_manager.name>/<version>/. training_start.sh sources this
# file and exports the variable, and perso/training_config.yaml reads it through
# exp_manager.exp_dir (${oc.env:NEMO_EXP_DIR,./nemo_experiments}).
#
# Point it at an external drive. A checkpoint for this model is ~3.2 GB and
# exp_manager keeps the top 5 plus a -last plus a ~2.4 GB .nemo export, so a
# single run eats about 22 GB. Keeping that off the system disk is the point.
#
# The real .env is gitignored because the path contains the username, which
# must never be committed. Only this placeholder version is tracked.
#
# training_start.sh refuses to start if the parent directory does not exist,
# so an unmounted drive fails loudly instead of silently filling the system
# disk with multi-GB checkpoints.
NEMO_EXP_DIR=/media/<your-user>/<your-drive>/nemo_experiments
